  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why this exists",
      "items": [
        "A sleeping PC cannot hear Telegram, and a PC woken by a task goes back to sleep as soon as the task ends",
        "Windows ends the listener's task whenever the PC sleeps or the network blips, and nothing started it again",
        "You are often away for weeks, so nobody is at the PC to notice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What keeps it reachable",
      "items": [
        "The listener holds the PC awake from 06:00 to 23:00",
        "The phone guard checks every 10 minutes and starts the listener again if it is not running",
        "Every scheduled command (refresh, daily run, research, weekly report) and the watchdog check first, and the watchdog tells you",
        "The task no longer waits for a network, so a Wi-Fi blip does not end it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How you know it works",
      "items": [
        "One Daily check message at 10:50: the PC is on and listening",
        "No message means the PC is off or has no internet; nothing on the PC can tell you that",
        "The 19:00 reminder comes only when jobs are waiting, and the 20:00 question only when a company-website job is unanswered"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "What it cannot do",
      "items": [
        "A PC that is shut down cannot be woken by any task; leave it on, or switch it on before you leave",
        "The listener only starts the apply run; every job still waits for your Yes tap, and silence means no",
        "It obeys only your own Telegram chat; an /apply older than 10 minutes is ignored"
      ]
    }
  ]
